{
  "rules": [
    "Strong upward-trend underestimation: when the last 5–10 days show a clear rally (higher highs / higher lows), the model stays too flat and underprices the entire path. Apply an additive uplift that grows with horizon (small at days 1–3, large by days 10–30).",
    "Horizon-dependent bias: errors increase with forecast length (near-term mildly low; 2–4 weeks materially low). Use a ramp correction (e.g., +X at day 1 increasing roughly linearly/exponentially to +Y by day 30).",
    "Regime shift lag: after a breakout to a higher price regime, the model behaves mean-reverting and anchors to the old level (~high-60s/low-70s), while realized prices rebase into mid/high-70s and 80s. Add a level-shift adjustment when price crosses and holds above recent resistance for several days.",
    "Volatility/acceleration miss: during fast moves, the model underestimates slope (daily change). If recent momentum (e.g., 5-day return) is strongly positive, increase projected daily drift proportionally rather than reverting to the mean.",
    "Late-horizon compression: model forecasts converge to a narrow band (~68–72) regardless of conditions; true outcomes remain dispersed and higher in rallies. Widen the forecast distribution and raise the terminal level when trend/momentum indicators are positive."
  ]
}
